m from the northeast to do that  ever when they called our name to final  it was like new york new york they're  like  who from new york is is in a final here  so we certainly broke the mold a little  bit on that first year down there and  that ended up be becoming our catalyst  that was like wow we're kind of onto  something we're pretty good at what we  do and rob is like why don't we take  this the next step soon there was a  fixed location in brooklyn and just a  few months ago they opened an enormous  new pig beach outpost in queens  here is a beer garden meets barbecue  meets burgers but with the jumbotron and  the size of the facility what we do at  pig beach we want families to come in we  want to bring the kids we want people to  spend the day come watch a game  sample all our food  pork pig pork is pig here family and  friendship are the focus just as much as  food  in part because of what happened three  years ago  one of their chefs jeff michener matt  abdu's brother-in-law was at work when  he developed a brain aneurysm he died at  the age of 36 leaving behind a wife and  16 month old child  his pig beach brothers hold frequent  fundraisers in his honor within our  career of cooking there is basically  the best way that we know how to honor  somebody or to show our love and  affection is is to cook how does he  still affect this place he well he's  within me he's everywhere what do you  think he would think of what you've  built now i think he is super jealous  that he's not here to be a part of it i  was going to say the same thing because  he wishes you would be here this is this  was his dream  pig beach's brisket sandwich is named  for jeff  part of a menu that includes all the  staples you ready for a snack i am ready  for a snack prepared the pig beach way  you can smell that porky goodness from  everything smell that oh my god i'm a  baby and for a treat  that's for you thank you how am i  joining you  oh yeah  oh man  what we want to do is we always approach  every single piece of food that we cook  with that sort of chef mindset you  seeing this are you seeing this  we're looking at it is how can we  perfectly balance sweet salty fatty acid  umami getting all these flavors  perfectly balanced to make the best bite  possible i could eat these all day  believe it or not you do end up getting  sick of it after you cook them every  single day but  i can't imagine it but sometimes doing  the barbecue all you want the other day  is a nice salad  don't worry about that what about that  later favorite barbecue item ribs  ribs  brisket  are we eating all of that today and more  more indeed  our dish spread included  barbecue buffalo wings with alabama  white sauce  pig beaches smash burgers  collard greens yankee sausage with  cherry pepper relish  salt and pepper brisket  tangy vinegar pulled pork  greek seasoned smoked lamb shoulder with  new york city white sauce  those amazing peach and honey glazed  ribs  and an entire 120 pound pig  it's like barbecue heaven you ready yeah  it's a little bit of the taste of the  belly of this pig we're gonna pull it  out just like that and you're gonna see  this amazing bacon  just pull  right out just so effortlessly all juicy  twist it up  and you have your first bite  this is mine whole hot pork belly  indoctrination into the team oh my god  it doesn't get any better than that does  it insane right  melting in your mouth in your mouth the  pork belly the whole hog that's arguably  one of the best bites on the pig and one  of the things you're not allowed to  submit into the box for judging because  it's like cheating because it's too good  that's the ultimate expression of  barbecue cooking a whole animal  that's like  true  barbecue you're talking that's a 24-hour  commitment for one item of food how to  manage a fire managed to smoke how you  get flavor into a whole animal and it's  some of the best times because we're up  all night together so the the  storytelling the drinking i mean you're  up all night feeding fire and watching  that  your baby in that cooker  do you believe that someday new york or  this area can be  regarded as highly as places in texas or  tennessee i think it's already getting  there yeah because there's a lot of  great talented people  that are pursuing this bug of barbecue  and it's becoming more and more of a  national  cuisine versus when it was solely  restricted to the southern south states  or the midwest  there is another location opening by the  way in louisville and you're  i mean i'm sorry  this is the chicken sandwich on the  plate we have the chicken sandwich spare  ribs coleslaw beans uh collard greens  and then over here there's the wider  shot of wow i have the tea we got  brisket which is good luck to you yeah  you cut the sandwich and let's see here  we go

